think Surveyed image/: the text-paint family is mature (solid, paint_placed, paint_placed_clipped, paint_line, paint_paragraph) yet every paragraph stacks LEFT-set only. Alignment is the crux-first Lindy rung -- every text surface needs it, it composes the already-proven wrap + paint, and it is pure geometry where left is a strict superset of today.
think Confirmed font5x7_ascii glyph_advance = cell_w + 1 = 6 > cell_w = 5, so a line's painted box (width-1) sits strictly inside its advance width -- an alignment shift within the slack stays inside the paragraph box the up-front check proved.
think Grew paint_paragraph_aligned(mode: Align{left,centre,right}) as the full body with a per-line sideways offset = slack (right) / slack/2 (centre) / 0 (left); rewrote paint_paragraph to delegate with .left, so the two share one routine (single-stranded) and left reproduces the pre-alignment paint byte-for-byte.
think Zig reserves `align`, so the parameter is `mode` -- caught by the first build, fixed, rebuilt GREEN.
obs Proof composes alignment from the strict single-line painter: built expected right/centre canvases by painting each wrapped line at its own offset, then matched paint_paragraph_aligned byte-for-byte; centre and right change exactly the same pixel count as left (alignment shifts ink, adding none, dropping none); right-set differs from left-set (the short line moved) while the widest line holds its origin under every alignment.
